  "attestation": "Second Phase 0 change on top of d332108 (which is already accepted): in an Alembic site alembic.json is Alembic's own file (SITE-TYPE-CONTRACT §4), so MS3 no longer applies the v0.12-era local manifest rule (alembic-manifest) there. The site test is the gate's existing host mode, factored into records/host.mjs alembicHost (no .git and a .coursewerk-host.json from Alembic) and reused by hostLogFailures (behaviour unchanged); the snapshot carries it as `site` (runner -> module_host), the host record itself still stays out of the files and the snapshot id is unchanged. A local package, or a host record inside git, keeps the rule. Reviewed all 76 required items again for the new statements: CHANGELOG updated; the docs, templates, site and skills say nothing about the manifest rule in site mode and need no change. Tests: the 36 required plus genchem-phase0 (new req.format.site-manifest test), runner, stable-modules, site-import, site-export, redteam-r1/r2/r6-visible/r6-reviews/r7-judged, wiring-modules, d49, job-release, system-index: 701/701 passed (xargs --test-concurrency=2, COURSEWERK_FRAMES=installed). On the course copy MS3 now raises 8 blocking (6 real heading-level jumps in 6 assessment guides; 2 '$$' counts that are two adjacent inline spans and render correctly), no manifest items: gate column B 1,520 -> 1,513.",
